    <string name="oem_detected">%1$s (your phone)</string>
    <string name="background_other_phones">Menus differ between models and software versions. If you cannot find an option, search for it in Settings.</string>
    <string name="oem_vivo_title">vivo and iQOO</string>
    <string name="oem_vivo_steps">1. Settings &gt; Battery &gt; Background power consumption management: allow ZapFlick.\n2. Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Autostart: turn ZapFlick on.\n3. In recent apps, pull the ZapFlick card down to lock it.</string>
    <string name="oem_tecno_title">Tecno, Infinix and itel</string>
    <string name="oem_tecno_steps">1. Phone Master or Settings &gt; Battery: set ZapFlick to no restrictions.\n2. Phone Master &gt; Autostart manager: allow ZapFlick.\n3. In recent apps, long-press the ZapFlick card and lock it.</string>
    <string name="oem_xiaomi_title">Xiaomi, Redmi and POCO</string>
    <string name="oem_xiaomi_steps">1. Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Manage apps &gt; ZapFlick &gt; Battery saver: choose No restrictions.\n2. On the same page, turn Autostart on.\n3. In recent apps, long-press the ZapFlick card and tap the lock icon.</string>
    <string name="oem_samsung_title">Samsung</string>
    <string name="oem_samsung_steps">1. Settings &gt; Battery &gt; Background usage limits: remove ZapFlick from the sleeping lists and turn off putting unused apps to sleep.\n2. Settings &gt; Apps &gt; ZapFlick &gt; Battery: choose Unrestricted.\n3. In recent apps, tap the ZapFlick icon and choose Keep open.</string>
